{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal multiprofile setup using scvi_n200 RNA encoder (more complex than pca_n2000) and resnet50 images with avgpool aggregation and concat fusion. Validation accuracy of 0.6315 (vs 0.6186 in config_018) suggests multimodal integration may provide marginal improvement over previous multimodal baselines, though it underperforms the RNA-only scvi_n200 baseline (0.6501). The relative impact of RNA encoder complexity versus image data addition, as well as interactions with aggregation/fusion strategies, remains uncertain without direct comparisons to alternative configurations."
}

